  "text": "Board of Elections | Board of Elections\nSkip to main content\nAn official website of Mecklenburg County.\nHere\u2019s how you know\nOfficial County websites use MeckNC.gov\nMeckNC.gov\nwebsites belong to official departments or programs of the Mecklenburg County government.\nSecure MeckNC.gov websites use HTTPS\nA\nlock\n(\nLock\nA locked padlock\n) or\nhttps://\nmeans you\u2019ve safely connected to a MeckNC.gov website. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites.\nResidents\nServices for Me\nBirth and Death Certificates\nMarriage and Divorce Records\nBrowse by Department Listing\nHealth and Human Services\nPark and Recreation\nAccessibility\nGIS & Mapping\nHow do I?\nPay Taxes and Fees\nView Arrest Records\nVote in Mecklenburg County\nWork for Mecklenburg County\nRecycle in Mecklenburg County\nUse the Accessibility Toolbar\nBusinesses\nServices for Businesses\nBusiness Taxes and Fees\nConstruction, Building and Land Development\nEconomic Development\nFood and Facilities Sanitation\nLodging, Childcare and Institutions\nWaste and Recycling\nDoing Business with the County\nVendor Enrollment and Opportunities\nVendor Resources and Support\nGovernment\nCounty Government\nAbout Mecklenburg County\nCounty Manager's Office\nBoard of County Commissioners\nCounty Budget\nCounty Departments\nCommunity Relations\nHow do I?\nDo Business with the County\nRequest a Public Record\nRequest a Speaker\nWatch a BOCC Meeting\nJoin a County Advisory Board or Committee\nPublic Notices\nSearch\nSITE MENU\nSite navigation\nBoard of Elections\nInformation On Upcoming Elections\nInformation About Voter Registration\nInformation for Candidates\nData and Downloads\nAbout the Board of Elections\nDepartment Leadership\nOffice Address\nBusiness Office\n741 Kenilworth Ave.\nSuite 202\nCharlotte, NC 28204\nBusiness Hours\nMon-Fri 8 a.m. - 5 p.m.\nContact Info\n704-336-2133\n[email protected]\nEarly voting statistic for Nov General 2026\nView site totals by day\nFact: In NC, if an Election Worker Writes on Your Ballot, It Does Not Invalidate It\nSocial media posts and other communications suggest that if an election worker writes on your ballot, it would invalidate it. In North Carolina, this is\nfalse.\nThese posts have been circulating for years and have resurfaced recently in many N.C. counties.\nThey are still false.\nElection workers often do write on ballots for different reasons as required by law.\nBoard of Elections\nManaging the election process within Mecklenburg County.\nGeneral Election Information\nResources\nCheck Registration & Sample Ballot\nRequest a Mail-In Ballot Online\nOffices on the Ballot for 2026 General Election\nLook-Up Districts by Address\nVolunteer to Work the Polls\nCounty Voter Demographics\nCampaign Finance Reports\nUpdate Your Registration\nEarly Voting Sites and Hours For 11/3/2026 Election\nList of Acceptable Voter Photo IDs\nNCSBE 2026 Judicial Voter Guide\nDetailed Instructions to Vote By Mail\nEvents\nView all Events\nTuesday, October 20, 2026\nAbsentee Board of Elections Meeting\n741 Kenilworth Ave, Charlotte, NC, 28204 |\nEvent\nTuesday, October 27, 2026\nAbsentee Board of Elections Meeting\n741 Kenilworth Ave, Charlotte, NC, 28204 |\nEvent\nMonday, November 2, 2026\nAbsentee Board of Elections Meeting\n741 Kenilworth Ave, Charlotte, NC, 28204 |\nEvent\nTuesday, November 3, 2026\nBoard of Elections - Board Meeting\n741 Kenilworth Ave, Charlotte, NC, 28204 |\nEvent\nLatest News\nView All News\nFriday, July 24, 2026\n2026 Official General Election Notice\nNews\nWednesday, August 16, 2023\n10 Facts About NC's Photo ID Requirement for Voting\nNews\nShow More\nView All News\nI want to learn more about...\nRegistering to Vote in Mecklenburg\nVoter Registration\nVoting in Mecklenburg County\nVoting Info\nRunning for Public Office\nCandidate Information\nOther Important Information\nFind Your Elected Officials\nFind information about the people who represent you.\nFind Your Elected Officials\nMecklenburg County District Maps\nAll County Districts were redrawn in 2021 based on 2020 U.S. Census Data. These new districts directly impact who you are allowed to vote for based on your home address.\nDistrict Map Options\nMunicipalities\nLearn more about Mecklenburg County cities and towns.\nCounty Municipalities\nHistorical Data\nMecklenburg County provides historical election data for your to examine and download for research purposes.\nElection Data\nNeed additional help?\nContact Us\n704-336-2133\n[email protected]\nVisit Us\n741 Kenilworth Ave., Suite 202\nCharlotte, NC 28204\nMail Us\nMecklenburg County Board of Elections\nP.O. Box 31788\nCharlotte, NC 28231\nBack To Top\nWebsite Information\nBrand Guidelines\nPrivacy and Legal Notices\nSocial Media Accounts\nWeb Accessibility Statement\nGetting Started\nDepartment Directory\nEmployment\nHHS Services\nPay Taxes\nWatch BOCC Broadcasts\nAssistance\nAccessibility Toolbar\nAccessibility\nCharMeck 311\nPublic Record Requests\nRequest a Speaker\nOffice Address\nBusiness Office\n741 Kenilworth Ave.\nSuite 202\nCharlotte, NC 28204\nBusiness Hours\nMon-Fri 8 a.m. - 5 p.m.\nContact Info\n704-336-2133\n[email protected]\nStay connected\nSign-up for email to stay connected to County news.\nSign up\nYour email address\nEmployee Access",
